sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/kimura-fixation-probability> a delphi:Concept, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Kimura fixation probability of a mutant allele (Lean 4, kernel-checked)" ;
    dct:description "In a neutral absorbing chain on 0..M copies, including the exact Wright-Fisher chain, a mutant present in i copies is eventually fixed with probability i/M." ;
    dct:source "On the probability of fixation of mutant genes in a population (1962)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1093/genetics/47.6.713> ;
    skos:notation "u(p) = \\frac{1-e^{-4N_e s p}}{1-e^{-4N_e s}}; neutral limit u(p) = p, so a new mutant fixes with probability 1/(2N)" ;
    skos:definition """theorem fixedBy_tendsto (i : Fin (M + 1)) :
    Tendsto (fun t => C.fixedBy t i) atTop (nhds (C.fixationProbability i))"""^^delphi:lean4 ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    delphi:leanDeclaration "Delphi.NeutralChain" ;
    delphi:leanTheorem "Delphi.NeutralChain.fixedBy_tendsto", "Delphi.NeutralChain.fixedBy_sub_le" ;
    delphi:leanVerified "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    skos:scopeNote "Neutral case only (s = 0), exact Wright-Fisher chain rather than the diffusion approximation." ;
    rdfs:comment "Status: kernel-checked (Lean 4 accepted the module with zero sorry and standard axioms only). Not expert-validated. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/main/lean/Delphi/Kimura.lean>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/kimura-fixation-probability> dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/kimura-fixation-probability> ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-kimura-fixation-probability> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-kimura-fixation-probability> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Lean 4 kernel accepted Delphi.NeutralChain.fixedBy_tendsto with zero sorry and standard axioms, and rejected 2 deliberately broken variant(s)" ;
    dct:description "Build receipt. Lean (version 4.35.0, x86_64-w64-windows-gnu, commit eb6cafb7290e8bd5f2937522d8d804f58f02bafc, Release); toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0; Mathlib v4.35.0 (56a005855ea17e0b0958f73ec801ae140b0a1679). lake build exit 0 in 5.2 s with 0 errors; 0 sorry in lean/Delphi/Kimura.lean (413 lines). #print axioms for Delphi.NeutralChain.fixedBy_tendsto, Delphi.NeutralChain.fixedBy_sub_le: Classical.choice, Quot.sound, propext only (Lean's standard axioms; no sorryAx). Mutation evidence (lean/mutate.mjs, 2026-10-31T15:49:26.326Z): 2 deliberate change(s) to the statement or the model were each rejected by the compiler: [kimura-limit-wrong] Statement changed so the fixation probability of i copies tends to i/(M+1) instead of i/M. Rejected with 3 error(s): kimura-limit-wrong.lean:264:2: error: Type mismatch: After simplification, term [kimura-escape-dropped] Model hypothesis removed: the chain no longer has to be able to leave interior states (escape := True). Fixation then need not happen, so the limit theorem must fail. Rejected with 1 error(s): kimura-escape-dropped.lean:156:14: error: Function expected at Controls: 4 of 4 unmodified modules accepted by the same command." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/kimura-fixation-probability> ;
    rdfs:comment "This evidence item establishes that the stated theorem follows from the stated model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/main/lean/mutations.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/main/lean/Delphi/Audit.lean> .
}

